<!--
  Who may wear the good plate.

  Inside the Society, recoilArmor and pulseArmor belong to Golds - plus the small
  number of Obsidians and Grays who have been given a title, which is how the
  Society says out loud that it has decided to trust someone. Everyone else fights
  in duroArmor, and the gap between 0.42 and 1.24 sharp is what that decision is
  worth in a firefight.

  SAME SHAPE AS THE RAZOR RESTRICTION, and for the same reason. Vanilla cannot
  express "this armour is reserved to a caste": apparel gating is by body part,
  layer, gender and developmental stage, and none of those know anything about who
  a pawn is. So enforcement lives in Source/RimRising/CasteArmor.cs and this file
  is the belief it enforces.

  IT IS A LAW, NOT A LAW OF PHYSICS. It binds only pawns whose ideoligion actually
  holds the precept. The Rising armours whoever it likes - that is its whole
  argument, and enforcing the Society's rule on the people rejecting it would be
  perverse.

  NOTE WHAT IS NOT GATED HERE: the caste TINT. Armour takes its wearer's Color on
  both sides, because the Rising has not stopped caring what Color someone is - it
  cares enormously. A Gold's plate is gold to say the hierarchy is right; Darrow's
  is red to say it is not. Same mechanic, opposite argument.
-->
<Defs>

  <IssueDef>
    <defName>RR_ArmorBearing</defName>
    <label>armor bearing</label>
    <iconPath>UI/Issues/RR_ArmorBearing</iconPath>
  </IssueDef>

  <!-- =============================== the Society ========================== -->

  <PreceptDef>
    <defName>RR_ArmorBearing_Restricted</defName>
    <issue>RR_ArmorBearing</issue>
    <label>plate for the proven</label>
    <description>Recoil plate is not clothing. It is the Society's confidence, cut to fit, and it is issued to those who have earned the right to survive - Golds by birth, and the rare Obsidian or Gray who has been handed a title for service that could not be ignored.\n\nEveryone else is given duroSteel and told it is enough. For the work they are expected to do, it is.</description>
    <impact>Medium</impact>
    <displayOrderInIssue>10</displayOrderInIssue>
    <associatedMemes>
      <li>RR_ColorHierarchy</li>
    </associatedMemes>
    <conflictingMemes>
      <li>RR_ColorEquality</li>
    </conflictingMemes>
  </PreceptDef>

  <!-- ============================= the resistance ========================= -->

  <PreceptDef>
    <defName>RR_ArmorBearing_Earned</defName>
    <issue>RR_ArmorBearing</issue>
    <label>plate for the fighting</label>
    <description>Armour goes to whoever is going to be shot at. It is not a statement about their blood and it never was - it is plate, and plate stops things.\n\nThere is never enough of it, so it goes to the ones who have already proven they will walk toward the guns. That is a different kind of rank, and it is earned rather than inherited.</description>
    <impact>Low</impact>
    <displayOrderInIssue>20</displayOrderInIssue>
    <associatedMemes>
      <li>RR_ColorEquality</li>
    </associatedMemes>
    <conflictingMemes>
      <li>RR_ColorHierarchy</li>
    </conflictingMemes>
  </PreceptDef>

</Defs>
